Batiste — licensing
===================

Batiste is open-core. This repository contains two bodies of code under two
different licences, and each package declares its own `license` field in its
`package.json`. Those per-package declarations are authoritative. This file
states the same division in one place.

Copyright (c) 2025-present Cachola Tech Ltda (CNPJ 62.014.963/0001-00),
Sao Paulo, Brazil. All rights reserved except as expressly granted below.


1. MIT-licensed packages
------------------------

The MIT licence reproduced in section 3 applies to, and only to, the following
packages in this repository:

    packages/aidk                 packages/audit
    packages/auth                 packages/code
    packages/connectors           packages/core
    packages/graph                packages/gvs
    packages/memory               packages/rls
    packages/router               packages/scope
    packages/sign                 packages/transport

The grant is by enumeration. A package is MIT-licensed only if it is named in
the list above.


2. Proprietary packages and everything else
-------------------------------------------

All other content in this repository — including but not limited to
packages/atrium, packages/cli, packages/credential-preflight,
packages/marketplace, packages/parallel, packages/pitch-integrity,
packages/repo-hygiene and packages/ui-consistency — is proprietary and
source-available. It is published so that it can be read, audited and
evaluated. No licence to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute,
sublicense or sell it is granted by this file or by its presence in a public
repository. Commercial terms: jardhel@cachola.tech.

Third-party dependency notices are reproduced in NOTICE.


